# GitHub Issues (CLI)

Created: 2026-02-02 09:33 UTC  
Last reviewed: 2026-02-02 09:33 UTC

## Summary
Documented the exact `gh` commands used to create, close, and delete issues for the EnderAI repos.

## Commands Used
Create issue:
```sh
/tmp/gh/gh_2.86.0_linux_amd64/bin/gh issue create \
  --repo al-exe/EnderAI-frontend \
  --title "Test issue" \
  --body "Test issue created via gh for project auto-add verification."
```

Close issue (keeps history):
```sh
/tmp/gh/gh_2.86.0_linux_amd64/bin/gh issue close 1 --repo al-exe/EnderAI-frontend
```

Delete issue (removes it):
```sh
/tmp/gh/gh_2.86.0_linux_amd64/bin/gh issue delete 1 \
  --repo al-exe/EnderAI-frontend \
  --yes
```

## Notes
- This session used a locally downloaded `gh` binary under `/tmp/gh/`. If you install `gh` normally, the command may be just `gh ...`.
